<div class="text-center">
<h1 class="display-4">Purpose of the Workout Diary</h1>
<p><strong>The Workout Diary</strong> is designed to help you track your workouts, monitor your progress, and stay motivated on your fitness journey. 
    Whether you're a beginner or an experienced athlete, this tool allows you to log your exercises, sets, repetitions, 
    and other important details to keep you accountable and focused on your goals.</p>
    <img class="Motivations" src="~/content/img/motivation.png" alt="Motivation" />
    <p>
        <strong>The purpose of exercise and why health matters</strong>
        Exercise is about so much more than building muscle or losing weight. It is an investment in your entire life – in how you feel, how you think and how you cope with everyday life. When we move regularly, we not only strengthen our body, but also our mental resilience, our self-esteem and our ability to handle stress. Exercise is one of the most powerful tools we have to create a life of energy, balance and long-term health.

        In an era where many people sit still for most of the day, physical activity becomes a crucial counterbalance. The body is built for movement, and when we exercise, everything from blood circulation and immune system to sleep quality and concentration improves. Regular exercise reduces the risk of cardiovascular disease, type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure and depression – and it does not take extreme workouts to have an effect. Continuity always beats intensity.

        But exercise is also about creating a stronger relationship with yourself. Feeling that you can do more than you thought. Building discipline, routines and pride in your own development. Every session, no matter how small, is a step towards a better version of yourself. That’s why exercise often becomes a lifestyle – not because you have to, but because you notice how much better life feels when your body gets what it needs.

        Health is the whole. It’s the balance between physical strength, mental clarity, recovery and good habits. It’s about taking care of yourself in a way that lasts over time. Exercise is one of the most important building blocks of that whole, and when you combine movement with good nutrition, sleep and recovery, you create a solid foundation for a healthier and more sustainable life.

        <strong>In short:</strong>
        The purpose of exercise is to give you a life where you can do more, feel better and feel strong – both in body and mind.
    </p>
</div>